{"resourceIdentifier":"3678","resourceName":"Chia Tai AWMS GHG Mitigation Project in Guangdong Province","description":"Chia Tai AWMS GHG Mitigation Project in Guangdong Province (hereafter referred to as the project) introduces new animal waste management systems (AWMSs) to treat the manure from 15 Existing swine farms in Zhanjiang, Guangdong Province, which are owned by Guangdong Zhanjiang Chia Tai Swine Industry Co., Ltd. The purpose of the project activity is to treat the manure and wastewater to avoid methane emissions generated in the baseline uncovered anaerobic lagoons.\r\nThe specific treatment process of this newly constructed project is as follows: All the manure and wastewater are collected and then be separated first. The solid will be treated in aerobic composting system and the organic fertilizers will be produced, which will be distributed to local farmers for free and the surplus will be sold in domestic market. The waste water enters an anaerobic treatment system (enclosed) for reaction and biogas generates. The biogas is captured for electricity generation, with surplus biogas destroyed through the flaring system (if any). The sludge would be produced from anaerobic digestion and the effluent is supplied to the farmers living around free for agriculture irrigation as organic fertilizers together with other fermentation wastes produced in the project. The electricity generated are all used by the AWMSs and the swine farms, and hence the GHG emission reductions generates from the avoidance of methane emissions from the enclosed treatment system and the electricity generation.","location":{"latitude":21.388500,"longitude":110.026200},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-09-21","endExclusive":"2022-10-22","endInclusive":"2022-10-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3678"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Guangdong Province"}]}],"participatio